  {
   "id": "wsdUsNh-DAAJ",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2015-08-19T17:42:32Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Rqtl-disc] Type of crossing",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "It&#39;s best not to treat an RIL population as an F2,\r<br>but R/qtl will omit any heterozygous genotypes in an RIL population.\r<br>\r<br>When loading the data with read.cross, you can use the argument crosstype to indicate the cross type, either crosstype=&quot;risib&quot; or crosstype=&quot;riself&quot;.\r<br>\r<br>  mycross &lt;- read.cross(&quot;csv&quot;, file=&quot;myfile.csv&quot;, crosstype=&quot;risib&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>Alternatively, you can use the convert2riself() or convert2risib() functions\r<br>\r<br>  mycross &lt;- read.cross(&quot;csv&quot;, file=&quot;myfile.csv&quot;)\r<br>  mycross &lt;- convert2risib(mycross)\r<br>\r<br>karl\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>&gt; On Aug 19, 2015, at 12:24 PM, Daniany Adorno &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">daniany....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I can use the F2 intercross to crossing populations RIL?\r<br>&gt; if not possible, as it changed the type of crossing on R / qtl?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thank you.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "&gt; -- \r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R/qtl discussion&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rqtl-disc+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rqtl...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; Visit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/rqtl-disc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/rqtl-disc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448044604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw262FyrPF-okseq6-jWF4vP\">http://groups.google.com/group/rqtl-disc</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448044605000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CP7aB9whoppMZV5d5FVW4\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>\r<br>"
